	"_comment": "Ship parts (scripts/sim/ship_parts.gd ShipParts; DESIGN_LIVING_WORLD.md M4). A model's parts are every entry whose from_tier is at or under its tier and whose categories (if any) include its category: about 5 on a tier-1 boat, 10 at tier 2, 20 at tier 3, 30 at tier 4 and 45-50 on the giants. Each part has a condition 0 to 1 on the ship (Ship.parts); the ship's maintenance figure is the weighted mean (weight). Wear spreads over the parts by rate x weight (a hull fouls steadily, electrics fail in jumps). group: hull (fouling and plating: fuel), propulsion (propeller, shaft, rudder: speed), engine and electrics (breakdowns), deck (cargo gear, winches: port time), systems (the rest: a little of everything). major parts are only put right in drydock (at a shipyard port or a hub with the Drydock facility); the others are fixed during ordinary port stops. upgrade: one per part, bought in drydock for cost (a share of the ship's list price), with effects as factors on fuel, speed, breakdowns and dock (port time); better ones come with technology (M5).",
